  "findings_addressed": {
    "M01": "the bounded canonical payload is staged under the pinned descriptor parent, flushed and fsynced there, and only a successful durable staging is published under the canonical name with a no-overwrite hard link; unpublished staged bytes are explicitly non-authoritative and rejected by the canonical loader; a failed staging leaves no canonical success, returns a blocked receipt with unknown storage and preserves the failed evidence that a replay cannot overwrite; the honest accounting counts both retained entries; the crash durability limit is stated",
    "M08": "the source, storage and cleanup evidence has complete typed shared validators used by both the execution phase and the scoring entry point; the source carries the full typed descriptor identity, size, hash and a run-root bound path; the release carries the actual bounded native proof; the execution emits the uncertainty booleans explicitly and the scoring requires the literal False; only a published canonical receipt is authority",
    "NM01": "one final local send-admission guard after all controlled callbacks revalidates the ownership, the typed parent proof identity, validity interval and current remaining capacity; the reservation and the attempt charge happen immediately before the submit with no unchecked callback in between; the cumulative reservation never exceeds the admitted capacity or 34; there is no refund and no retry",
    "NM02": "the same guard refuses a send past the phase deadline and a non finite, boolean or decreasing clock; the cooperative checks are kept and the mandatory parent process supervision stays UNIMPLEMENTED_PRODUCT_GATE0_BLOCKER"
  },
